MarkText 0.23.0: license, source and configuration

The unmodified Linux x86_64 release archive is downloaded from:
https://github.com/marktext/marktext/releases/download/v0.23.0/marktext-linux-0.23.0.tar.gz
SOURCE.json records its SHA-256 digest. solve.sh extracts the release unchanged,
removes the temporary archive from the installation and drops the unused
Chromium sandbox helper's set-user-ID bit. Product file contents are unmodified.
Source for the release is available at https://github.com/marktext/marktext/tree/v0.23.0.

MarkText is licensed under MIT; LICENSE contains the complete upstream text.
LICENSES/electron.txt and LICENSES/chromium.txt preserve the bundled Electron
and Chromium/component notices. chromium.txt contains the full textual content
of LICENSES.chromium.html with HTML presentation removed; the original remains
in the release archive and extracted product. LICENSES also preserves the
notices for bundled ced, font-list, keytar and ripgrep. Other Node module
notices remain embedded in app.asar and the extracted native module resources.

The local start.sh and jail.py configure an English X11/D-Bus/AT-SPI session,
private HOME/XDG/Electron data under DATA_DIR, renderer accessibility and
in-process GPU execution. Document arguments are forwarded to the existing
application instance. jail.py establishes Landlock before starting the product
and refuses to start if confinement cannot be established. These launchers are
separate from upstream code. No writable installation directory is required.

This task is not affiliated with or endorsed by the MarkText authors.

The GUI starts in the document outbox so file dialogs open a readable exchange
directory while the installation root remains non-enumerable.
